ility in repair cycles; process change shows management response but suggests previous approach was insufficient for actual demand","iso":"2026-09-08","paper_title":"Housing Revenue Account Revenue and Capital Budget Monitoring Report 2026/27, Quarter 1","paper_url":"https://melton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s32571/32571.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Housing Revenue Account Revenue and Capital Budget Monitoring Report 2026/27, Quarter 1","paper_url":"https://melton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s32571/32571.pdf","headline":"Q1 revenue overspend of \u00a331k being managed through reserve contribution reduction","detail":"Forecast year-end revenue overspend of \u00a331k against approved budget. Council is managing this by reducing planned contribution to Regeneration & Development Reserve while maintaining statutory working balance of \u00a31m, indicating tight headroom for further adverse variance.","category":"reserves","matters":"Shows council can operate within planned reserve flexibility but has limited tolerance for further cost pressures or income volatility","figures":"\u00a331k forecast overspend against net cost of services of \u00a31,008,220; working balance \u00a31m","quote":"Overall, this will result in a reduced contribution to the Regeneration & Development Reserve in order to maintain the approved working balance of \u00a31m.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Housing Revenue Account Revenue and Capital Budget Monitoring Report 2026/27, Quarter 1","paper_url":"https://melton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s32571/32571.pdf","headline":"Rental income shortfall of \u00a310k from void properties carried into 2026/27","detail":"High number of voids carried forward is anticipated to cause a \u00a310k shortfall in rental income. Council expects improved void repair processes will help control future losses.","category":"income","matters":"Rental income is fundamental to HRA viability; voids create income leakage beyond repair costs and indicate cash generation risk","figures":"\u00a310k shortfall","quote":"Due to the high number of voids being carried forward into 2026/27 it is anticipated that there will be a shortfall in rental income of \u00a310k.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Housing Revenue Account Revenue and Capital Budget Monitoring Report 2026/27, Quarter 1","paper_url":"https://melton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s32571/32571.pdf","headline":"Repairs & Maintenance overspend of \u00a353k due to higher than budgeted void rates","detail":"Properties became void at higher rates than expected in 2025/26, with repairs incomplete at year-end and flowing into 2026/27. The council has changed procurement from contracted pricing per property to a schedule of rates, aiming to bring spending under control as void numbers fall back to normal levels.","category":"demand","matters":"Indicates forecasting gap and operational volatility in repair cycles; process change shows management response but suggests previous approach was insufficient for actual demand","figures":"\u00a353k overspend","quote":"a number of voids had not completed by 31 March flowing through into 2026-27. This is, to a degree due to a larger than budgeted number of properties becoming void during the previous year. Action has been taken to review the process by which voids are dealt with regarding repairs moving from a contracted price per property to a schedule of rates pricing.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix A - Corporate Performance, Risk and Feedback report","paper_url":"https://melton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s32577/32577.pdf","headline":"Local government reorganisation confirmed: Melton will cease to exist as a council in April 2028","detail":"In July 2026, the government selected a model creating two unitary councils in Leicester, Leicestershire and Rutland, with Melton merging into one of them. The council will cease to exist from April 2028. Significant uncertainty remains over staffing, assets, liabilities, and local accountability.","category":"governance","matters":"Lenders need to know whether liabilities, contracts, and pension obligations will transfer and on what terms. The transition creates execution risk and the council's ability to deliver commitments beyond 2028 is eliminated.","figures":"Effective date April 2028; decision made July 2026","quote":"In July 2026, the Government selected its chosen model for LGR within LLR - to establish two unitary councils.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix A - Corporate Performance, Risk and Feedback report","paper_url":"https://melton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s32577/32577.pdf","headline":"Waste collection site has drainage defects with legal proceedings underway","detail":"Initial drainage works at Melton's waste site were found to be substandard after investigation, with incorrect concrete specifications and failure to meet operational requirements. Legal proceedings are ongoing to address these deficiencies. Severn Trent and the Environment Agency have raised enforcement concerns.","category":"other","matters":"This affects continuity of a critical council service (waste collection) and creates unquantified financial and legal exposure. Enforcement action could disrupt operations or require emergency spending.","figures":"Not specified; matter assessed 14 July 2026","quote":"Initial drainage works were undertaken on site; however, subsequent investigations revealed that these works were substandard, involving incorrect concrete specifications and failing to account for operational requirements. Legal proceedings are ongoing to address these deficiencies.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-08"},"name":"Melton","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-22","since_iso":"2026-08-23","distress":false,"headline":"Q1 revenue overspend of \u00a331k being managed through reserve contribution reduction","lead":"Shows council can operate within planned reserve flexibility but has limited tolerance for further cost pressures or income volatility","also":["38 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit and Standards Committee on 2026-09-22","n_findings":39,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Housing Revenue Account Revenue and Capital Budget Monitoring Report 2026/27, Quarter 1","top_paper_url":"https://melton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s32571/32571.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":149,"news_drafts_total":3}}